      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I strongly advise against trying to downplay the incident with misleading language, as this can lead to more significant trust issues and legal risk down the line.  A transparent and responsible narrative is generally the best strategy for crisis management with the press.\n\nFocus on what you are *doing* to fix it, such as \"unauthorized access to a misconfigured storage system that is now secured and being actively managed by a third-party to investigate the scope of the data involved, which appears to be limited to 50 email addresses in a specific, non-sensitive context.\"\n\nAlways prioritize factual honesty to mitigate the \"negligence\" claim, but emphasize proactive, decisive action to demonstrate commitment to user trust.",
